From: Pulse diagnostics
Subject: [PATCH] Show what a crafter can actually reach, and unblock the advance

Three changes, one build.

1. PulseStatus printed only wood/ore/food, so leather, ingots and wares were
   invisible whatever their value -- a town could be swimming in ore with no
   ingot to its name and the readout looked the same. Now prints every kind,
   and beside each the amount no resident has claimed, which is the only part
   Buy can take from the town's own stores.

2. "X holds 6 of it" was share.TotalValue() -- a resident's total across all
   kinds, with the kind never named. Now names each kind, and prints the purse,
   which is the number that decides whether a crafter can buy at all.

3. Advance refused a top-up to any crafter holding a single coin. Buy only
   reaches for an advance when the purse is already short of one unit's price,
   so a crafter sitting on 2gp with ore at 3gp could neither buy nor be topped
   up -- permanently. Now tops up anyone short of a unit.

Plus: Thoughts.Ask passed the stockpile count with no unit attached, so "The
town holds 220" came back from the model as "a town of 220 people" (Britain has
57). The unit is now in the prompt.

--- a/src/Pulse/Commands/PulseCommands.cs
+++ b/src/Pulse/Commands/PulseCommands.cs
@@ -236,8 +236,27 @@
             );

-            from.SendMessage(
-                $"    stores: wood {settlement.Stockpile[ResourceKind.Wood]} " +
-                $"ore {settlement.Stockpile[ResourceKind.Ore]} " +
-                $"food {settlement.Stockpile[ResourceKind.Food]}"
-            );
+            // Every kind, not just the three that are gathered: a town can be swimming
+            // in ore and have no ingot to its name, and the old three-kind line hid
+            // exactly that. The bracketed figure is what no resident has claimed, which
+            // is the only part Buy can spend from the town's own stores.
+            var stores = string.Empty;
+
+            foreach (var kind in new[]
+                     {
+                         ResourceKind.Wood, ResourceKind.Ore, ResourceKind.Food,
+                         ResourceKind.Leather, ResourceKind.Ingot, ResourceKind.Goods
+                     })
+            {
+                var total = settlement.Stockpile[kind];
+                var unclaimed = total;
+
+                foreach (var (_, claim) in settlement.Ledger.Shares)
+                {
+                    unclaimed -= claim[kind];
+                }
+
+                stores += $"{kind.DisplayName()} {total}({unclaimed}) ";
+            }
+
+            from.SendMessage($"    stores, (unclaimed): {stores}");

@@ -266,7 +285,30 @@

                 if (owners <= 5)
                 {
-                    var who = World.FindMobile(owner)?.Name ?? "the town";
-                    from.SendMessage(0x3B2, $"    {who} holds {share.TotalValue()} of it");
+                    var holder = World.FindMobile(owner);
+                    var who = holder?.Name ?? "the town";
+                    var what = string.Empty;
+
+                    foreach (var kind in new[]
+                             {
+                                 ResourceKind.Wood, ResourceKind.Ore, ResourceKind.Food,
+                                 ResourceKind.Leather, ResourceKind.Ingot, ResourceKind.Goods
+                             })
+                    {
+                        if (share[kind] > 0)
+                        {
+                            what += $"{share[kind]} {kind.DisplayName()}, ";
+                        }
+                    }
+
+                    // The purse is the whole question for a crafter: Buy is capped by it,
+                    // and Advance only tops one up when it is short of a single unit.
+                    var purse = holder == null ? -1 : Purse.Balance(holder);
+
+                    from.SendMessage(
+                        0x3B2,
+                        $"    {who} holds {(what.Length == 0 ? "nothing, " : what)}" +
+                        $"purse {(purse < 0 ? "n/a" : purse.ToString())}"
+                    );
                 }
             }
--- a/src/Pulse/Economy/Workshop.cs
+++ b/src/Pulse/Economy/Workshop.cs
@@ -217,6 +217,6 @@
             Thoughts.Ask(
                 crafter,
                 $"Cannot get {input.DisplayName()} to work with. The town holds "
-                + $"{_settlement.Stockpile[input]} and is "
+                + $"{_settlement.Stockpile[input]} {input.DisplayName()} and is "
                 + (_settlement.Upkeep.Hungry ? "going hungry." : "fed for now."),
                 _settlement.Upkeep.Hungry ? 3 : 2
@@ -491,7 +491,11 @@
     {
         var advance = unitPrice * PulseConfig.OpeningStockBatches;

-        if (Purse.Balance(crafter) > 0 || !_settlement.Economy.CanAfford(advance))
+        // Was "> 0", which refused an advance to any crafter holding a single coin --
+        // including one holding less than one unit's price, who could then neither buy
+        // nor be topped up, for the rest of his life. Buy only reaches for an advance
+        // when the purse is already short of a unit, so this is exactly that gap.
+        if (Purse.Balance(crafter) >= unitPrice || !_settlement.Economy.CanAfford(advance))
         {
             return 0;
         }
